{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/Ad_for_Adjunct_Faculty2021.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty Teaching Opportunities",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty Teaching Opportunities. Part-Time Faculty Teaching Opportunities  \nLander University is hiring part-time faculty in many disciplines taught at the university. If you \nhave a master’s degree including 18 graduate hours in a discipline, experience using a Learning \nManagement System (LMS), and interest in teaching a class at the college level, we would like \nto explore this possibility with you.  To indicate your interest, please submit a letter of \napplication, your vita, and unofficial transcripts for all degrees received to Melissa Thompson at \nmthompson@lander.edu. (mail to: mthompson@lander.edu) \n \n \nLander University is a tobacco-free campus. All final candidates are subject to successfully \ncompleting background requirements.  \nLander University is committed to equal opportunity employment and being an employer of \nchoice. Lander believes that corresponding differences within the faculty and staff, whether \nbased on ethnicity, race, gender, religion, age, or other experiences, are tremendous assets to the \nrole of Lander as an educational institution and within the community, region, and state. \nMoreover, Lander is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. As a result, it is the \npolicy and commitment of Lander that it will not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, \nnational origin, age, disability or other protected characteristics. AA / EOE / ADA / Title IX "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/therapeutichorsemanshipadjunct-8-26.pdf": {
      "title": "Therapeutic Horsemanship Adjunct",
      "description": "Therapeutic Horsemanship Adjunct. Therapeutic Horsemanship Adjunct"
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/university_supervisors_job-8-26.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-Time University Supervisors of Student Teacher Candidates",
      "description": "Part-Time University Supervisors of Student Teacher Candidates. University Supervisors of Student Teacher Candidates \n \nThe College of Education invites applications for University Supervisor positions. University Supervisors \nobserve and evaluate teacher candidates during the semester-long student teaching experience. \nUniversity Supervisors must be a certified teacher evaluator in the state of South Carolina “Expanded \nADEPT 4.0” teacher effectiveness assessment system. The College of Education will provide Expanded \nADEPT 4.0 training at no cost for those selected to serve as university supervisors who are not already \ncertified. Student teacher supervisors are compensated on a per teacher candidate basis. Some travel costs \nare reimbursed. \n \nMinimum Qualifications: Master’s degree with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hours of coursework \nin the teaching related activities is required. Prior PK-12 experience required; university teaching \nexperience preferred. \n \nSend electronically or via mail: letter of application, vitae/resume, and unofficial copy of transcripts to \nCandice Rodgers, crodgers@lander.edu, College of Education, CPO Box 6011, 320 Stanley Avenue, \nGreenwood, SC 29649. Official transcripts and a satisfactory background check will be required upon \nhiring. "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/Part-time_Adjunct-Laboratory-Clinical-Instructor-Application2023.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-Time Laboratory/Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Part-Time Laboratory/Clinical Instructor. LANDER UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF NURSING \nADJUNCT CLINICAL/LABORATORY INSTUCTOR APPLICATION \n \nThe William Preston Turner School of Nursing invites applications for adjunct (part-time) laboratory/clinical \ninstructor positions for various clinical specialties. Our clinical days are Tuesdays and Thursdays throughout the \nacademic year (August-April). \n \nRESPONSIBILITIES: \n• Assumes campus/clinical laboratory supervision role \n• Assists in teaching activities within designated courses under the leadership of the course coordinator \n• Maintains currency of nursing knowledge and skills in area of preparation \n• Carries out instructional designs developed by course coordinator \n• Enhances clinical knowledge and skills in area of teaching focus \n• Expands nursing knowledge and skills in area of preparation \n• Functions under the supervision of a course coordinator who maintains overall course responsibility \n \nQUALIFICATIONS: \n• Master’s degree in nursing preferred; Bachelor’s degree in nursing required \n• Unencumbered RN licensure in South Carolina \n• BLS certification \n• A minimum of two years clinical practice as a professional registered nurse \n• Evidence of effective clinical practice that includes experience with formal and informal teaching of patient \ngroups or student groups, and/or of licensed nurses’ groups \n• Must have a satisfactory drug screen and background check \n• Must meet immunization and health screening requirements \n• Must maintain Professional Liability insurance \n• Must have a driver’s license \n \nHOW TO APPLY: \nInterested individuals may apply by completing the Laboratory/Clinical Instructor Application and submitting the \napplication with a resume and the names/phone numbers of three references to: \n \nGinny Leopard \nAdministrative Assistant \nLander University \nWilliam Preston Turner School of Nursing \n320 Stanley Avenue \nGreenwood, SC 29649 \nPhone: 864-388-8396 \nFax: 864-388-8122 \ngleopard@lander.edu \n \n \n*Applicants for employment are required to undergo a background investigation in our selection and hiring process \nto help determine the applicant’s/employee’s overall employability. The final candidate(s) must successfully satisfy \nthe employment background, drug and health screen requirements prior to entering the workforce A Summary of \nYour Rights Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act is available for your review on the Lander University Human \nResources web site, \nhttp://www.lander.edu/Business-Administration/Human-Resources/employment/Employment-Opportunities.aspx. \nLANDER UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF NURSING \nADJUNCT CLINICAL/LABORATORY INSTUCTOR APPLICATION \n(All fields must be complete for consideration) \nPLEASE PRINT \n \n \nNAME   \nLast Middle Initial First \n \n \nEMAIL   \n \n \n \nHome Address City State Zip \n \n \nHome phone:    Cell phone:   Work:    \n \n \nE-mail address:   Current Employer:   \n \n \nHighest Academic Degree:   Year Highest Degree Earned:    \n \n \nAdditional Training/Certification/Degree \n \n \n \nPLEASE INDICATE ALL CLINICAL AREA(S) THAT YOU WOULD BE INTERESTED IN: \n \n  Wellness Nursing   Physical Assess   Basic Nsg Strat   Med Surg \n \n  Childbearing   Mental Health   Crit Care Nsg   Ped Nsg \n \n  Leadership   Community Nsg   OTHER   \n \n \nAVAILIBILITY:  Tuesday   Thursday   Either \n \n \n \nI certify the above information is true to the best of my knowledge. \n \n \nApplicant Signature Date "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/eshp-adjunct-faculty-7-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science. Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science and Human Performance \nThe College of Nursing, Human Performance and Health Sciences invites applications for adjunct \nfaculty (part-time) to teach undergraduate courses in the Department of Exercise Science and \nHuman Performance. \nThe department is seeking qualiﬁed instructors to teach activity-based and foundational courses \nthat promote lifelong physical activity and wellness. Areas of need may include one or more of the \nfollowing: \n• Swimming\n• Tennis\n• Badminton\n• Golf\n• Racquetball\n• Soccer\n• Volleyball\n• Basketball\n• Ultimate Frisbee\n• Weight Training\n• Cardio Yoga\n• Walk/Jog Aerobics\n• Dance Aerobics\n• Wellness for Life Activity\nAdditional opportunities may be available to teach introductory Exercise Science or Human \nPerformance courses based on departmental needs and applicant qualiﬁcations. \nCourses are taught primarily in person on the Lander campus, with limited opportunities for online \ninstruction. \nMinimum Qualiﬁcations: Master's degree in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Physical Education, \nHealth Promotion, or a closely related ﬁeld. Relevant professional certiﬁcations and/or \ndemonstrated expertise in one or more activity areas are desirable. University teaching experience \nis preferred. \nPlease submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae or résumé, and unofficial transcripts \nelectronically to Chelsey Driver at cdriver@lander.edu or by mail to: \nChelsey Driver \nCollege of Nursing, Human Performance and Health Sciences \nLander University \nCPO Box 6026 \n320 Stanley Avenue \nGreenwood, SC 29649 \nOfficial transcripts and a satisfactory background check will be required upon hire. "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/ad-for-assistant-professor-of-eshp-3-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science. Assistant Professor of Exercise Science  \nDepartment of Exercise Science and Human Performance  \nApplications are invited for a tenure-track position in the Department of Exercise Science \nand Human Performance. This full-time, nine-month position will begin on August 10, 2026.                                                                           \nFaculty responsibilities: This position requires teaching a variety of undergraduate and \ngraduate Exercise Science-related courses, which may include exercise physiology, clinical \nexercise physiology, physiology of aging, exercise testing and prescription, principles of \nstrength and conditioning, exercise science internship/practicums, and/or biomechanics, \nbased on the academic background and experience of the candidate and departmental \nneed.   \nRequired: The successful candidate will have an earned doctorate at the time of \nappointment in Exercise Physiology, Exercise Science, or a related area. Preferred: \nTeaching experience at the university level, strong communication and interpersonal skills, \nexperience developing and teaching online courses, American College of Sports Medicine \n(ACSM) certiﬁcation or National Strength and Conditioning Association (NSCA) Certiﬁed \nStrength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) certiﬁcation, accreditation experience with \nCAAHEP and/or CASCE.   \nSend a letter of application; curriculum vita; unofficial transcripts of undergraduate and \ngraduate course work; statement of teaching philosophy for exercise science; the names, \naddresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references to:   \n \nDr. Bruna Lynch  \nAssociate Professor, Undergraduate Exercise Science Program Coordinator  \nDepartment of Exercise Science and Human Performance  \nblynch@lander.edu  \n(864) 388-8280  \nLander University  \n320 Stanley Avenue  \nGreenwood, SC 29649  \n \nElectronic submission of materials to blynch@lander.edu is preferred.  \n \nLander University is a tobacco-free campus. All ﬁnal candidates are subject to successfully \ncompleting background requirements. Note: The University generally does not sponsor an \nH-1B visa.   "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/adjunct-faculty-for-pathophysiology-2025.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Pathophysiology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Pathophysiology. Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science  \nThe College of Nursing, Human Performance, and Health Science invites applications \nfor adjunct faculty (part-time) in our School of Nursing with expertise in \npathophysiology and experience teaching beginning nursing students how to apply \nknowledge of pathophysiology in scenario style assessments.  The course is taught in-\nperson on Tuesday and Thursday with one section offered at 8:00 AM and another at \n10:00 AM on our Lander campus, with some limited opportunities to teach online \ncourses.  \nMinimum Qualiﬁcations: Master’s degree in nursing or relevant discipline. University \nteaching experience preferred. Send letter of application via mail, vitae/resume, and \nunofficial copy of transcripts to Ginny Leopard, gleopard@lander.edu, 320 Stanley \nAvenue, Greenwood, SC 29649. Official transcripts and a satisfactory background \ncheck will be required upon hiring. "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/Science_Lab_Instructor_Positions_Available2021.pdf": {
      "title": "Science Lab Instructors",
      "description": "Science Lab Instructors. Science Lab Instructor Positions Available  \nLander University is hiring part-time instructors for introductory science labs taught at the \nuniversity. If you have a bachelor’s degree in biology, chemistry, physics, or a closely related \nfield and are interested in supervising a science lab at the college level, we would like to explore \nthis possibility with you. Lab sections are offered at a wide range of times. To indicate your \ninterest, please submit a letter of application, your vita, and unofficial transcripts for all degrees \nreceived to Melissa Thompson at mthompson@lander.edu. (mail to: mthompson@lander.edu) \nLander University is a tobacco-free campus. All final candidates are subject to successfully \ncompleting background requirements.  \nLander University is committed to equal opportunity employment and being an employer of \nchoice. Lander believes that corresponding differences within the faculty and staff, whether \nbased on ethnicity, race, gender, religion, age, or other experiences, are tremendous assets to the \nrole of Lander as an educational institution and within the community, region, and state. \nMoreover, Lander is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. As a result, it is the \npolicy and commitment of Lander that it will not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, \nnational origin, age, disability or other protected characteristics. AA / EOE / ADA / Title IX \n "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/ad-for-math-up-to-2-positions-4-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor of Mathematics. Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor of Mathematics (non-tenure track)  \nLander University  \n \nThe Department of Mathematics at Lander University invites applications for up to two full-\ntime, non-tenure track positions at the rank of Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor, \nbeginning August 2026.  \n \nMinimum Qualiﬁcations: Candidates must hold at least a master’s degree in Mathematics, \nStatistics, or a closely related ﬁeld, with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the \ndiscipline. Applicants who hold a Ph.D. may be considered for appointment at the rank of \nTeaching Assistant Professor.  \n \nPreferred Qualiﬁcations: Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate a strong \nrecord of effective teaching, particularly with diverse student populations and varying \nlevels of academic preparedness.  \n \nResponsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to teach general education and \nintroductory mathematics courses, with a standard teaching load of 30 credit hours per \nacademic year. In addition to teaching, all faculty members are expected to contribute \nservice to the department, college, and university, and any other duties as assigned.  \n \nReview of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is ﬁlled.  \n \nTo apply, please submit the following materials electronically to: Dr. Jennifer Yates, Dean of \nthe College of Science and Mathematics jyates1@lander.edu cover letter, curriculum vitae, \nstatement of teaching (including a description of any evidence-based instructional \npractices and approaches to fostering student engagement and success), graduate and \nundergraduate transcripts, and contact information for three references.  \n \nLander University is a tobacco-free institution. All ﬁnal candidates are subject to \nsuccessfully completing background requirements. Note: The university generally does not \nsponsor an H-1B visa. An affirmative action/equal opportunity employer/Title IX. \n \nFor more information about the University and Greenwood, SC, please visit the Lander \nUniversity website, lander.edu. "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/ad-for-visiting-assistant-professor-of-environmental-chemistry-03-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Environmental Chemistry",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Environmental Chemistry. Visiting Assistant Professor of Environmental Chemistry \nLander University \nApplications are invited for a visiting position in Environmental Chemistry to begin August \n2026.  \nPhD in Environmental Chemistry or related ﬁeld required.   \nA strong commitment to excellent teaching is essential.  Ability to teach undergraduate \nchemistry and environmental science classes for both majors and non-majors, including \nlectures and laboratories, required.   \nPreference will be given to candidates providing evidence of a record of excellent teaching.  \nAfter the ﬁrst year, there is a possibility that this position may convert into either a \npermanent teaching position, or into a tenure-track line.    \nContract period is nine months.  \nNormal teaching load is 15 contact hours each semester.  \nSalary determined by experience.   \nSend letter of application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial \ntranscripts, and names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three \nreferences, by email in Microsoft Word or pdf format, to: \nDr. Jennifer Yates at jyates1@lander.edu.   \nScreening of applications will begin April 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is \nﬁlled.   \nLander University is a tobacco-free campus.  All ﬁnal candidates are subject to \nsuccessfully completing background requirements.   Lander University is committed to \nequal opportunity employment and being an employer of choice. Lander believes that \ncorresponding differences within the faculty and staff, whether based on ethnicity, race, \ngender, religion, age, or other experiences, are tremendous assets to the role of Lander as \nan educational institution and within the community, region, and state. Moreover, Lander is \nan Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. As a result, it is the policy and \ncommitment of Lander that it will not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, \nnational origin, age, disability or other protected characteristics.   AA / EOE / ADA / Title \nIX/EO/AA Employer  For more information about the University and Greenwood, SC, please \nvisit our homepage https://www.lander.edu/. "
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/ad-for-ap-biology-4-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology. Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology"
    },
    "https://www.lander.edu/about/offices-departments/human-resources/_documents/job-postings/visiting-lecturer-or-assistant-professor-of-biology-6-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Visiting Lecturer/Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Visiting Lecturer/Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology. Visiting Lecturer/Teaching Assistant Professor of Biology \nLander University \n   \nThe Position: The Department of Biology at Lander University, a public comprehensive \nuniversity in the Upstate region of South Carolina, comprises a cohesive and forward-\nthinking faculty who deliver an outcomes-based curriculum that has been carefully aligned \nwith the goals of the AAAS Vision and Change initiative.  This modern approach involves not \nonly our major programs but also courses for non-majors as well.  Our department seeks to \nhire a full-time, visiting lecturer or visiting teaching assistant professor to begin August 10, \n2026.  \n \nTeaching responsibilities will primarily be teaching lectures and labs for a general biology \ncourse for non-majors, but other opportunities may be possible depending on the \nsuccessful candidate’s background and the needs of the department. The ideal candidate \nwill share our passion for innovative teaching using high-impact practices.  Salary \ncommensurate with experience.  \n \nContract period is nine months. Normal teaching load is 15 contact hours each semester.   \n \nMinimum qualifications: Applicants must have at least a master’s degree in the biological \nsciences and demonstrable aptitude for teaching biology at the college level. Excellent oral \nand written communication skills are essential.    Application letters should explicitly \naddress the qualifications and desired aptitudes outlined above.     \n \nSend application letter; curriculum vitae; statement of teaching philosophy; copies of \nundergraduate and graduate transcripts; and the names, addresses, e-mail addresses, and \nphone numbers of three references in Word or PDF format to  \n \nDr. Jennifer Yates, Dean \nCollege of Science and Mathematics at jyates1@lander.edu.   \n \nReview of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.   \n \nAll final candidates are subject to successfully completing background requirements.  \nLander University is a tobacco-free campus.    Lander University is committed to equal \nopportunity employment and being an employer of choice. Lander believes that \ncorresponding differences within the faculty and staff, whether based on ethnicity, race, \ngender, religion, age, or other experiences, are tremendous assets to the role of Lander as \nan educational institution and within the community, region, and state. Moreover, Lander is \nan Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. As a result, it is the policy and \ncommitment of Lander that it will not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, \nnational origin, age, disability, or other protected characteristics.   AA / EOE / ADA / Title \nIX/EO/AA Employer For more information about the University and Greenwood, SC, please \nvisit our homepage https://www.lander.edu/. "
    }
  },
